\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The O-ISAC paradigm evolution. (A) RF-ISAC systems in sub-6 GHz/mmWave bands often face deployment-constrained spectrum and hardware limits, motivating a transition toward photonic carriers to pursue Tbps-class capacity and mm-scale sensing targets. (B) Optical-ISAC leverages the broad photonic spectrum ($\approx $28.3--845 THz), with implementations clustering in operational windows (telecom for fiber and NIR/visible/photonic-THz for wireless). The review taxonomy branches Optical-ISAC into fiber-based, free-space/photonic-THz, and VLC/LiFi modalities, each characterized by distinct signal models and dominant impairments.}}{2}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:fig1}{{1}{2}{}{figure.1}{}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {subsection}{\numberline {\mbox  {I-B}}The Optical Opportunity: A Vast and Untapped Frontier}{2}{}\protected@file@percent }
